cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "MLVM: deterministic RV64IMAFD execution over committed memory"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jianzhu
    family-names: Yao
    email: jy0246@princeton.edu
    affiliation: Princeton University
repository-code: "https://github.com/yao-jz/mlvm"
abstract: >-
  MLVM is a deterministic RISC-V RV64IMAFD emulator and proof-tooling laboratory.
  It executes floating-point instructions through a Go port of Berkeley SoftFloat,
  stores memory in a sparse Merkle tree, produces single-transition witnesses, and
  includes experimental Go and Solidity verification components. C and Rust
  numerical guests, including BERT-family workload demonstrations, run inside the
  fast interpreter. The proof components are research-grade and do not constitute
  a complete or audited dispute protocol.
keywords:
  - RISC-V
  - virtual machine
  - fraud proof
  - verifiable computation
  - machine learning
  - floating point
  - IEEE 754
  - determinism
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
references:
  - type: software
    title: "asterisc: RISC-V interactive fraud-proof technology"
    authors:
      - alias: protolambda
    repository-code: "https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/asterisc"
    license: MIT
    notes: >-
      MLVM's virtual machine is derived from asterisc. The RISC-V interpreter,
      merkleized memory, bisection tooling and Solidity mirror originate there.
  - type: software
    title: "Berkeley SoftFloat"
    authors:
      - given-names: John R.
        family-names: Hauser
    url: "http://www.jhauser.us/arithmetic/SoftFloat.html"
    notes: >-
      rvgo/comp is a hand port of Berkeley SoftFloat Release 3e to Go.
  - type: software
    title: "candle: minimalist ML framework for Rust"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/huggingface/candle"
    license: MIT
